# Journal vault privacy

When using `/journal`, journal-* skills, journal dashboard tools, or any DenMercs vault path under Google Drive:

## Allowed (only)

| Path | Use |
|------|-----|
| `…/DenMercs/Journal/**` | Weekly notes, Standup, On Call, `_dashboard` |
| `…/DenMercs/_Templates/**` | Read-only templates when creating a week / standup / on-call note |

Vault root itself is only a **prefix** for those joins — never a browse root.

## Forbidden

Do **not** Read, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write, or shell-list:

- `Private/`, `Workspace/`, `Knowledge/`, `BMO/`, `Music/`, `_Media/`, `Excalidraw/`, `copilot*`, or any other DenMercs folder outside the allowlist
- Broader Google Drive paths (`My Drive/**` outside DenMercs `Journal` / `_Templates`)
- OAuth token / secrets files under `_scripts` or `tools/.secrets` unless the user explicitly asked to debug auth

If a task seems to need a forbidden path → **stop and ask**. Do not “just check” those folders.

## Tools

Prefer `journal-*.cjs` / sync CLIs with `--vault`; they already scope to `Journal/`. Do not invent one-off scripts that walk the whole vault.
